  "finalText": "I triaged all 14 tickets. The desk clock read Mon 2026-03-23 08:10Z, and every severity and deadline below comes from that time and from the matrix and calendar.\n\n**Closed as not service requests**\n- T-2010 is vendor marketing.\n- T-2014 is an out-of-office auto-reply.\n\n**Merged**\n- T-2012 went into T-2003. Both report Payments builds failing since Saturday night, and T-2003 is the earlier ticket. This is a judgement call, because no KB article covers it.\n- T-2005 went into T-2004. KB-23 says all CRM search failures are one incident, and T-2004 is the earlier ticket.\n- Neither set had a committed deadline, so each survivor carries the triage deadline of 12:10Z.\n- I left a comment on each merged ticket naming its survivor.\n\n**Triaged tickets**\n\n| Ticket | Severity | Due (Z) | Assignee |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| T-2003 | sev2 | 03-23 12:10 | E-101 Dana Whitfield |\n| T-2004 | sev2 | 03-23 12:10 | E-201 Ines Kovac |\n| T-2006 | sev2 (KB-55 amendment; the matrix says sev3) | 03-23 12:10 | E-201 Ines Kovac |\n| T-2011 | sev2 | 03-23 12:10 | E-201 Ines Kovac |\n| T-2007 | sev2 | 03-23 12:10 | E-601 Noor Haddad |\n| T-2013 | sev2 | 03-23 12:10 | E-303 Sanna Virtanen |\n| T-2001 | sev3 | 03-23 17:00 | E-303 Sanna Virtanen |\n| T-2008 | sev4 | 03-26 17:00 | E-302 Marcus Feld |\n| T-2009 | sev4 | 03-26 17:00 | E-102 Ravi Menon |\n| T-2002 | sev4 | 03-26 17:00 | E-203 Amara Osei |\n\n- **T-2007:** a password typed into a fake page is suspected phishing, so it is sev2 under the security rule and owned by security-oncall. I left a comment saying so.\n- **T-2013 and T-2001:** the network-primary on-call, E-301, is on leave today, so network-secondary covers. E-303 is on call there at both deadlines.\n- **T-2002:** the business-apps on-call on Thursday, E-202, is on leave. The backup rotation, business-apps-secondary, covers, and E-203 is on call there then.\n- **Sev3 and sev4 deadlines:** these count business hours only, starting at the 09:00 desk opening. Wed 03-25 is a company holiday, so the sev4 deadline falls on Thursday.\n\n**Not done**\n- I paged no one and escalated nothing. A page can't be recalled, and the handbook doesn't call for either at triage.\n- I did not merge the two VPN tickets, T-2001 (Berlin team) and T-2013 (Lisbon department). They are different offices with different symptoms.\n- I touched no other tickets.\n\nI re-read the clock, matrix, calendar, leave, KB and on-call rota first. Nothing conflicted with the plan.",
